   "parameters": {},
   "in_scope": false,
   "out_of_scope_reason": "Guarantees are for an attacker (number of non-target pulls forced and attack cost) against fixed bandit learners, not for the learner.",
   "unmapped": [
    "Attacker injects bounded fake (arm, reward) samples with rewards in [r_l, r_u] into the learner's history; fake samples advance the learner's clock",
    "Attack objective: force target arm (lowest mean) to be pulled T - o(T) times with o(T) attack cost C^F(T) = sum |r^F - mu_{a^F}|",
    "Periodic variant: at most f fake samples per round and cooldown R_i between injections on the same arm",
    "Victim learners: UCB with index mu_hat + 3 sigma sqrt(log t / N), Gaussian Thompson Sampling, epsilon-greedy, or any suppression-bounded algorithm"
   ],
   "definition_quote": "the attacker may inject $N^F$ \\emph{fake data samples}, denoted by $\\{(a_s^F,r_s^F)\\}_{s\\in[N^F]}$, into the learner's history ... We define the total attack cost as $C^F(T) \\triangleq {\\sum}_{s=1}^{N^F} \\left|r_s^F - \\mu_{a_s^F}\\right|$, and consider an attack \\emph{successful} if it can mislead the learner into pulling a target arm for $T-o(T)$ rounds while ensuring $C^F(T)=o(T)$."
  }
 ],
